Emphasizing the disproportionate impact of the conflict on women, children, Indigenous and Afro-Colombian peoples, persons with disabilities, victims and survivors of conflict-related sexual and gender-based violence, and other vulnerable groups,

Reaffirming the importance of full, equal, meaningful and safe participation of women in all stages of peace processes, and of integrating a gender perspective as a cross-cutting issue into implementation, verification and reporting,

Recognizing the contribution of the Verification Mission to building confidence in the Comprehensive System for Truth, Justice, Reparation and Non-Repetition established under the Final Agreement, including through verification of compliance with sentences issued by the Special Jurisdiction for Peace,

Stressing the importance of comprehensive rural reform and implementation of the Ethnic Chapter, and of strengthening State presence and civilian institutions in conflict-affected territories,

Acknowledging the efforts of the Government of Colombia to seek broader peace through dialogue, and recognizing that ceasefire agreements are a step towards the development of comprehensive peace agreements,

Reiterating its willingness, at the request of the Government of Colombia and in agreement with the parties concerned, to consider mandating the Verification Mission to monitor and verify the implementation of a ceasefire agreement between the Government of Colombia and armed groups engaged in peace negotiations when the Secretary-General confirms that conditions, including a ceasefire with appropriate verification protocols, have been reached,

Expressing grave concern at the increase in illicit drug production and trafficking in Colombia and its impact on regional security, and underscoring the need for comprehensive and sustained counternarcotics efforts,

Recalling the importance of countering illicit drugs, including through crop substitution and alternative development, and of addressing the structural factors underlying the conflict, on the basis of shared responsibility,

Reaffirming its commitment to the sovereignty, independence, unity and territorial integrity of Colombia and the principle of non-interference in the internal affairs of States,

Emphasizing the primary responsibility and ownership of the Government of Colombia in the implementation of the Final Agreement and in the work of the Verification Mission, and reaffirming the need for the Mission to operate in close cooperation with and with the consent of the Government of Colombia,

Reaffirming the obligations of all parties under international humanitarian law and international human rights law,

Welcoming the role of the Special Representative of the Secretary-General in supporting the peace process and political dialogues,

