2. Reaffirms its full support for the comprehensive implementation of the Final Agreement, including rural reform, the Ethnic Chapter, gender provisions, transitional justice, reincorporation, and comprehensive security guarantees for former combatants and communities, with the full, equal and meaningful participation of Indigenous and Afro-Colombian peoples and their authorities;

3. Calls upon all parties to respect the Final Agreement and to ensure the safety and security of former combatants, their families, and communities;

4. Calls for the immediate cessation of all acts of violence against civilians, including sexual and gender-based violence, and attacks against human rights defenders, social leaders, women, children, Indigenous and Afro-Colombian peoples, former combatants, and members of the security forces, and calls for the immediate cessation of the recruitment and use of children by armed groups;

5. Urges the Government of Colombia to continue strengthening State presence and civilian institutions in conflict-affected areas, to take necessary measures for the protection of civilians, including displaced persons and support for their safe, voluntary and dignified return and reintegration, to facilitate safe, timely and unimpeded humanitarian access to all affected areas, and to combat impunity;

6. Calls upon all parties to allow and facilitate safe, rapid and unimpeded humanitarian access to affected populations, in accordance with international humanitarian law;

7. Calls for survivor-centred and gender-responsive protection and assistance, including safe and accessible referral to services for victims and survivors of conflict-related sexual and gender-based violence, and urges accountability for such crimes;

8. Calls upon the Government of Colombia to intensify efforts to address illicit drugs and related criminal economies through comprehensive and human rights-respecting approaches, including crop substitution, alternative development, interdiction and law enforcement, and encourages international cooperation and support in this regard, on the basis of shared responsibility;

