10. Calls upon the Government of Colombia and all relevant actors to ensure the safety, security and unimpeded access of the Verification Mission and its personnel, in coordination with the Government of Colombia and in accordance with the mandate;

11. Requests the Secretary-General to continue to report to the Council every 90 days on the implementation of this resolution and on the work of the Verification Mission, including on progress and challenges related to rural reform, the Ethnic Chapter and the Government of Colombia’s rapid response plan, verification of sentences issued by the Special Jurisdiction for Peace, protection of children, conflict-related sexual and gender-based violence, victims and survivors of conflict and access to reparations, humanitarian access, displacement and the cross-border humanitarian dimensions of the conflict, and the full, equal, meaningful and safe participation of women and youth and women’s organizations, and to include, where possible, age- and sex-disaggregated data in its reporting, and to ensure adequate gender expertise in the Mission’s work, and to continue to ensure efficient and effective use of the Mission’s resources, including through strengthened financial and human resources management, within the existing mandate;

12. Expresses its willingness to work with the Government of Colombia on the further extension of the mandate of the Verification Mission on the basis of agreement between the parties;

13. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

